e function\r\n\r\nit needs to get the correct parser_ref that has the requested class bc after https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/94871 there can technically be 2 parser_refs floating around and the analyzer needs to find the correct one\r\n\r\n`get_depended_parser_for` is intentionally not called in this function bc the parser its looking for may not be in the gdscript cache but it should be somewhere in the dependancy chain, and this function looks for it\r\n\r\nif it cant find it there is probably a bug somewhere else\r\n\r\nan alternate fix might be to look in the gdscript cache for it, without using `get_depended_parser_for` if it cant find it anywhere else","state":"CHANGES_REQUESTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98336#pullrequestreview-2381103839","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/98336","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98336#pullrequestreview-2381103839"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/98336"}},"submitted_at":"2024-10-21T06:58:55Z","commit_id":"4ee9f552ba3bf50c04ee2f2aacfbe3902858c4be"}]